From 80a1ba8c7ba2eaa6d7ba0182751df6f0a4217339 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shark rebrand <you@example.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 13:50:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Replace rocket branding with shark tail logo

- Launcher icon: adaptive-icon foreground (ic_launcher_foreground.xml) and
  all mipmap-*/ic_launcher_round.png redrawn as the shark tail on a purple
  (#7E57C2) circle, matching the earlier purple rebrand. Background color
  in values/ic_launcher_background.xml changed from #EE5444 to #7E57C2.
- In-app drawables: ic_rocket.png, ic_rocket_white.png,
  ic_rocket_white_60.png, ic_rocket_colour.png (mdpi/hdpi/xhdpi/xxhdpi) and
  the vector ic_rocket2.xml all redrawn as the shark tail. Filenames and
  R.drawable references are left untouched, so no Java/XML call sites
  needed to change -- only the underlying artwork.
    - White/white_60 variants keep serving as the notification icon,
      QS-tile icon, and disabled-state icon (eu.faircode.netguard.*,
      AndroidManifest.xml android:icon).
    - Colour variant keeps serving as the enabled-state icon in
      WidgetMain and the decorative icon across onboarding/info screens.
    - ic_rocket2.xml keeps serving as the tintable switch-thumb icon
      (styles.xml) and onboarding icons.
- Website assets: favicon.png and images/rocket.svg / rocket_black.svg /
  rocket_colour.svg redrawn as the shark tail (white/black/purple).
- README.md: removed the now-inapplicable 'rocket icon by Dave Gandy'
  credit line.

All shark artwork derived from the user-supplied purple_white_shark_logo.png
by alpha-masking against its white background, then vector-traced with
potrace for the two Android VectorDrawables (ic_rocket2.xml,
ic_launcher_foreground.xml) and the three website SVGs, and rasterised
per-density for the PNG assets.
